# Present-time readings come back after the window was covered (LIF-1 / S3D-1 on the Mac). A covered window discards presents; on the unfixed
# lookup the game-present count and the present-thread tickets drift apart for good, so every reading after the cover is "no reading"
# (perf blind=true) and Frame Drops freezes. The 12 s cover is longer than a perf window, so the second expect only sees frames from after the
# uncover. Windowed on the CLI host: the cover window has to sit on the game's Space.
# Pending: RED on the current code by design (the RED baseline of the fix); it moves to dm/verify/scenarios/ with the fix. The gate does not run it; the host suite parse-checks it.
name occlusion_readings
requires cli
save warlock
timeout 240
env DM_TEST_Q3D=0

enter_game
stick 1 0 frames=30
sleep 22
expect perf blind=false timeout=25
app cover
expect app state=occluded timeout=5
sleep 12
app uncover
expect app state=visible timeout=5
expect perf timeout=25
log skip the first window after the uncover: it still holds frames from before
expect perf blind=false timeout=25
quit
check no_red
check no_red_log
check no_event scale3d lv=1
